index 0000000..d7de28e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-razer-barracuda
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+What:           /sys/bus/hid/devices/.../headset_poweroff
+Date:           September 2026
+Contact:        Luis Atala <luis.atala@gmail.com>
+Description:
+                Write 1 to request power-off of the connected Barracuda X
+                (2022) headset. The operation is serialized with battery
+                queries, requires a validated link and existing diagnostic
+                transport, and restores the local route before returning.
+                A successful write means the request was sent, not that
+                physical shutdown has been confirmed. No acknowledgment is
+                required after shutdown; the command is never retried.
+                Link status still comes only from validated device reports.
+                The headset must be powered on with its physical button.
+                Concurrent operations may return EBUSY. Other input is
+                rejected. This attribute is write-only and root-owned;
+                administrators may grant access through local policy.
